1
00:00:15,310 --> 00:00:20,150
Unknown are the names
of the flowers that have been trampled

2
00:00:20,360 --> 00:00:25,610
Birds have fallen to the earth
and long for the wind

3
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:30,700
Prayers won't solve anything

4
00:00:30,910 --> 00:00:36,040
Only the will to fight
can change the here and now!

5
00:00:36,250 --> 00:00:41,340
O pigs who laugh at the resolve
to walk over corpses to move forward

6
00:00:41,540 --> 00:00:43,880
Livestock complacency? False prosperity?

7
00:00:44,090 --> 00:00:46,760
Give us the freedom of dying,
starving wolves!

8
00:00:46,970 --> 00:00:52,140
The humiliation of being caged
is what triggers us to fight back

9
00:00:52,350 --> 00:00:57,440
We hunters slaughter prey
beyond the castle walls,

10
00:00:57,640 --> 00:01:02,650
consumed with surging bloodlust,

11
00:01:02,860 --> 00:01:09,780
as our crimson bows and arrows
pierce scarlet holes into the twilight

12
00:01:31,988 --> 00:01:36,993
The World the Girl Saw: The Struggle for Trost, Part 2

13
00:01:37,350 --> 00:01:38,680
Hey!

14
00:01:38,890 --> 00:01:40,520
Hey! What's wrong, Armin?!

15
00:01:40,730 --> 00:01:41,690
Pull yourself together!

16
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:42,810
Hey!

17
00:01:43,020 --> 00:01:45,360
Armin! Hey, Armin!

18
00:01:45,570 --> 00:01:46,980
Hey!

19
00:01:47,740 --> 00:01:50,200
You with me?! You okay?!

20
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:53,370
Are you all right? Where's your squad?

21
00:01:53,570 --> 00:01:55,080
Squad...?

22
00:01:55,280 --> 00:01:56,950
Oh, man. Pull yourself together.

23
00:01:57,160 --> 00:01:58,830
Why are you all by yourself?

24
00:01:59,040 --> 00:02:01,830
Plus you're all wet and slimy...

25
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:04,170
What the hell happened?

26
00:02:09,550 --> 00:02:12,260
You're so useless! Just die already!

27
00:02:12,470 --> 00:02:14,550
- Whoa! Calm down, Armin!
- Damn it!

28
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:16,600
Where is everyone?!

29
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:19,140
Give it a rest, Conny.

30
00:02:19,350 --> 00:02:22,310
They've been wiped out. All but him.

31
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:25,110
Shut up! Armin hasn't said anything!

32
00:02:25,310 --> 00:02:27,150
Just look around. It's obvious.

33
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:30,320
We don't got any
more time to waste on him.

34
00:02:30,530 --> 00:02:32,570
Why is he the only one who's okay?!

35
00:02:32,780 --> 00:02:36,240
Beats me. Maybe they
thought he was a corpse?

36
00:02:36,450 --> 00:02:39,540
It sucks that they
ran into multiple Titans

37
00:02:39,750 --> 00:02:41,960
and that only this
underachiever made it out alive.

38
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:44,120
Eren and the others
worked hard for nothing.

39
00:02:44,330 --> 00:02:46,340
You bitch...

40
00:02:46,540 --> 00:02:48,800
Want me to make it
so you never talk again?!

41
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:50,380
Stop it, you two!

42
00:02:50,590 --> 00:02:53,010
We're all shaken up here!

43
00:02:53,220 --> 00:02:55,890
All our friends are suddenly
dying left and right!

44
00:02:56,100 --> 00:02:57,350
It's natural we're upset!

45
00:02:57,560 --> 00:03:03,100
That's my Christa!
Marry me when this is over!

46
00:03:03,310 --> 00:03:04,730
Yeah...

47
00:03:05,270 --> 00:03:07,730
She is clowning
around more than usual.

48
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:10,320
Anyways, we can't stay here.

49
00:03:10,530 --> 00:03:12,570
Can you stand, Armin?!

50
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:19,030
I'm sorry for the trouble.

51
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:22,040
I'll rendezvous with the rearguard.

52
00:03:22,250 --> 00:03:22,960
Hey...

53
00:03:23,160 --> 00:03:24,580
Armin!

54
00:03:28,210 --> 00:03:32,050
Let's go, Conny!
We've been ordered to advance!

55
00:03:36,470 --> 00:03:38,350
This is hell...

56
00:03:38,550 --> 00:03:42,770
No, it hasn't become hell.

57
00:03:42,980 --> 00:03:46,270
I was just mistaken until now.

58
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:50,610
This world has always been hell,
from the very start.

59
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:55,610
The strong prey on the weak.

60
00:03:55,820 --> 00:03:58,990
It's such a simple,
straightforward world.

61
00:04:00,030 --> 00:04:03,000
It's just, my friends...

62
00:04:05,830 --> 00:04:10,130
They tried to be strong in this world.

63
00:04:11,630 --> 00:04:15,550
They helped me, someone who was weak.

64
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:19,140
I couldn't bear it...

65
00:04:19,350 --> 00:04:23,680
They saw me as someone
who needed to be protected.

66
00:04:23,890 --> 00:04:26,060
I wanted to live
in this world like them...

67
00:04:26,270 --> 00:04:32,400
I wanted to be strong and stand
shoulder-to-shoulder with them...

68
00:04:40,700 --> 00:04:43,290
And this is the result.

69
00:04:43,490 --> 00:04:46,410
Because of me, Eren wound up...

70
00:04:58,260 --> 00:04:59,390
Hanna...

71
00:04:59,590 --> 00:05:01,640
What are you doing?

72
00:05:01,850 --> 00:05:02,930
Armin! Help!

73
00:05:03,140 --> 00:05:05,600
Franz isn't breathing!

74
00:05:05,810 --> 00:05:11,360
I've tried resuscitating him
over and over and over...

75
00:05:12,060 --> 00:05:13,900
...but it's not working!

76
00:05:14,110 --> 00:05:16,400
It's dangerous down here, Hanna.

77
00:05:16,610 --> 00:05:20,490
- You need to get on a roof...
- I can't just leave Franz like this!

78
00:05:20,700 --> 00:05:23,740
You don't understand, Hanna...

79
00:05:23,950 --> 00:05:25,580
Franz is...

80
00:05:32,750 --> 00:05:36,760
Please... stop this...

81
00:05:37,510 --> 00:05:38,720
I...

82
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:44,100
I can't take this anymore...

83
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:46,020
I can't...

84
00:05:51,310 --> 00:05:56,150
H-Hey, now! Don't you guys
realize how bad the situation is?!

85
00:05:56,360 --> 00:05:58,820
Yeah! That's why we're doin' this!

86
00:05:59,030 --> 00:06:01,280
And if you guys wanna live,
you'll give us some damn help!

87
00:06:01,490 --> 00:06:03,280
- The hell with that!
- It's gonna get stuck!

88
00:06:03,490 --> 00:06:06,490
- Letting people through comes first!
- We're all gonna get eaten standing here!

89
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:09,960
- What are you doing, soldier?!
- Go get 'em!

90
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:11,540
B-But...

91
00:06:11,750 --> 00:06:16,130
Just try it, small fry! I'm the boss
of this town's merchant association!

92
00:06:16,340 --> 00:06:18,260
Uhh, err...

93
00:06:18,460 --> 00:06:22,590
Who do you think pays for
the meals you soldiers shit out?!

94
00:06:22,800 --> 00:06:26,260
Do you have the money to
provide for the soldiers in this town?!

95
00:06:26,470 --> 00:06:27,930
Push, all of you!

96
00:06:28,140 --> 00:06:33,190
This cargo's worth more than you
can earn in your entire measly lives!

97
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:35,810
Help, and you'll be rewarded!

98
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:37,360
It'll be okay.

99
00:06:37,570 --> 00:06:41,700
Your dad's going to use his
cannons to make the Titans go away.

100
00:06:41,900 --> 00:06:43,610
Mom.

101
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:45,450
Over there.

102
00:06:56,170 --> 00:06:57,380
Push!

103
00:06:57,590 --> 00:06:59,460
Push if you don't wanna die!

104
00:06:59,670 --> 00:07:01,300
Stop! The children...!

105
00:07:06,220 --> 00:07:08,720
Damn! Why is it ignoring us?!

106
00:07:08,930 --> 00:07:11,390
It's an Abnormal!
No point trying to figure it out!

107
00:07:11,600 --> 00:07:14,810
It's fast! Not even we
elites can catch up to it!

108
00:07:15,020 --> 00:07:16,860
At this rate...!

109
00:07:36,830 --> 00:07:39,460
What... are you doing?

110
00:07:39,670 --> 00:07:41,550
Oh, perfect timing!

111
00:07:41,760 --> 00:07:44,380
Get these guys to help me!

112
00:07:44,590 --> 00:07:47,010
I'll make it worth your while!

113
00:07:48,890 --> 00:07:52,680
My comrades are dying as we speak.

114
00:07:52,890 --> 00:07:58,560
They're fighting and dying because
the citizens haven't finished evacuating.

115
00:07:58,770 --> 00:08:00,070
Of course they are!

116
00:08:00,270 --> 00:08:02,400
It's your duty to give your hearts

117
00:08:02,610 --> 00:08:05,450
to defend the lives
and property of the people!

118
00:08:05,650 --> 00:08:08,370
Don't go gettin' a big head now
that you freeloaders have somethin' to do

119
00:08:08,570 --> 00:08:10,410
after a century of uselessness!

120
00:08:19,080 --> 00:08:22,750
If you feel people dying for
other people is a matter of course,

121
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:28,550
then I'm sure you'll understand
that a single, precious life

122
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:31,180
can sometimes save
the lives of many as well.

123
00:08:31,390 --> 00:08:32,810
Just you try it!

124
00:08:33,020 --> 00:08:35,520
Your employer and I go way back!

125
00:08:35,730 --> 00:08:40,730
One word from me and
he'll be all over your sorry ass!

126
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:46,490
How can a dead body talk?

127
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:50,740
Wait!

128
00:08:54,540 --> 00:08:57,210
S-Sir!

129
00:08:57,410 --> 00:08:59,250
Pull the cart out.

130
00:09:08,180 --> 00:09:10,390
Thanks, lady!

131
00:09:10,590 --> 00:09:14,770
You really saved the day.
You have our gratitude!

132
00:09:40,370 --> 00:09:43,630
Good work taking it down,
Ackermann. Very impressive.

133
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:47,010
Thank you, Sir. However...

134
00:09:47,210 --> 00:09:51,510
I'm afraid I inadvertently dulled
my blades during the attack.

135
00:09:51,720 --> 00:09:53,930
I will be more careful next time.

136
00:09:54,930 --> 00:09:58,350
Just what have
you had to live through...?

137
00:09:58,560 --> 00:10:00,560
No, never mind.

138
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:09,990
Why am I reminded
of it at a time like this?

139
00:10:28,510 --> 00:10:30,130
Finished!

140
00:10:30,340 --> 00:10:31,880
Look, Mom!

141
00:10:32,090 --> 00:10:34,930
Oh, you did a great job, Mikasa!

142
00:10:35,140 --> 00:10:36,970
It's very nice!

143
00:10:38,020 --> 00:10:40,230
This style of embroidery has
been passed down in our clan

144
00:10:40,430 --> 00:10:42,770
from generation to generation.

145
00:10:42,980 --> 00:10:46,320
When you have a child,
it'll be your turn to pass it on too!

146
00:10:47,570 --> 00:10:49,440
How can I have a child?

147
00:10:49,650 --> 00:10:53,110
Err, why don't you ask your father that?

148
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:54,610
Well, Dad?

149
00:10:54,820 --> 00:10:57,780
Oh, uhh, I don't really know, either!

150
00:10:57,990 --> 00:11:00,700
Oh, I know!
Dr. Jaeger will be here any minute!

151
00:11:00,910 --> 00:11:03,250
Why don't we ask him?

152
00:11:05,880 --> 00:11:08,840
Oh, that must be him!

153
00:11:11,380 --> 00:11:12,800
Coming!

154
00:11:18,180 --> 00:11:18,970
Mikasa?

155
00:11:19,180 --> 00:11:22,810
Yes. She's about your age.

156
00:11:23,020 --> 00:11:27,150
There aren't many children
in these parts, so try to get along.

157
00:11:27,360 --> 00:11:29,860
That depends on how she acts...

158
00:11:30,070 --> 00:11:31,360
Eren.

159
00:11:31,570 --> 00:11:34,860
That attitude is why
you've only made one friend.

160
00:11:36,370 --> 00:11:37,950
Are they not home?

161
00:11:39,030 --> 00:11:40,120
Mr. Ackermann!

162
00:11:40,330 --> 00:11:42,160
It's Jaeger!

163
00:11:44,500 --> 00:11:46,330
Is anyone home?

164
00:11:48,630 --> 00:11:50,130
What's wrong?

165
00:11:51,590 --> 00:11:53,550
What is it, Dad?

166
00:12:02,020 --> 00:12:03,310
Too late.

167
00:12:03,520 --> 00:12:04,600
Eren.

168
00:12:04,810 --> 00:12:09,110
Have you seen the girl..
Mikasa... anywhere nearby?

169
00:12:09,310 --> 00:12:10,650
No.

170
00:12:10,860 --> 00:12:12,280
I see...

171
00:12:13,490 --> 00:12:16,660
I'll get the Military Police
and have them conduct a search!

172
00:12:16,860 --> 00:12:18,700
You'll wait at the foot of the mountain.

173
00:12:18,910 --> 00:12:21,410
Is that clear, Eren?!

174
00:12:22,540 --> 00:12:23,950
Eren!

175
00:12:30,460 --> 00:12:34,880
Hey. Are you sure she'll actually sell?

176
00:12:35,090 --> 00:12:38,010
We even went and killed her
parents before running off with her...

177
00:12:38,220 --> 00:12:41,140
Take a look at her face.

178
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:47,060
Looks nice, but she's
still just a kid. She ain't for me.

179
00:12:47,270 --> 00:12:49,860
I'm not asking about your tastes.

180
00:12:50,060 --> 00:12:52,110
She's an "Oriental."

181
00:12:52,320 --> 00:12:55,490
There used to be different types
of humans, you see.

182
00:12:55,690 --> 00:12:58,030
Long ago, some people
fled a place called the Orient

183
00:12:58,240 --> 00:13:00,030
and sought refuge inside the walls.

184
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:02,780
She's the last descendant of that clan.

185
00:13:02,990 --> 00:13:05,540
We're gonna take her to the
underground market in the capital

186
00:13:05,750 --> 00:13:08,540
and auction her off to those old perverts.

187
00:13:08,750 --> 00:13:12,880
All the other Orientals have died out,
so she'll go for a pretty hefty price.

188
00:13:13,090 --> 00:13:16,420
Her old man didn't
look like an Oriental to me.

189
00:13:16,630 --> 00:13:18,380
She ain't pureblooded.

190
00:13:19,590 --> 00:13:22,760
That's right! The mom
was the really valuable one!

191
00:13:22,970 --> 00:13:24,600
But you had to freak out and kill her!

192
00:13:24,810 --> 00:13:27,640
I-I couldn't help it! She put up a fight!

193
00:13:27,850 --> 00:13:30,600
That all you got
to say for yourself?! Huh?!

194
00:13:36,110 --> 00:13:36,990
Dr. Jaeger!

195
00:13:37,190 --> 00:13:39,030
We've been expecting...

196
00:13:51,830 --> 00:13:53,840
Hello. Pardon the intrusion.

197
00:13:59,930 --> 00:14:01,840
Just take it nice and easy,

198
00:14:02,050 --> 00:14:05,430
unless you want
your head split open with this.

199
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:08,730
This broad's crazy!

200
00:14:08,930 --> 00:14:10,440
Mikasa! Run!

201
00:14:10,640 --> 00:14:12,100
Huh? M-Mom...

202
00:14:12,310 --> 00:14:14,230
Hurry, Mikasa!

203
00:14:15,150 --> 00:14:17,150
Uhh...

204
00:14:17,360 --> 00:14:18,400
Dad...?

205
00:14:18,610 --> 00:14:21,700
Damn it! I've had enough of your crap!

206
00:14:34,460 --> 00:14:37,420
What the hell?!
I said only kill the dad!

207
00:14:37,630 --> 00:14:39,800
Don't look at me!
She's the one who...!

208
00:14:40,010 --> 00:14:42,220
Save your excuses! Go get the kid!

209
00:14:42,430 --> 00:14:43,840
Huh?!

210
00:14:46,560 --> 00:14:47,390
Hey.

211
00:14:47,600 --> 00:14:49,890
You better behave yourself.

212
00:14:51,180 --> 00:14:53,980
Or else... this!

213
00:15:05,030 --> 00:15:06,450
Cold...

214
00:15:17,460 --> 00:15:19,460
Excuse me...

215
00:15:20,300 --> 00:15:21,720
Hold it, kid!

216
00:15:21,920 --> 00:15:24,050
How did you find this place?!

217
00:15:24,260 --> 00:15:25,840
Err, uhh...

218
00:15:26,050 --> 00:15:31,310
I got lost in the forest,
and then, umm, I saw a cabin, so...

219
00:15:36,020 --> 00:15:40,570
You know kids shouldn't
wander around the forest all alone.

220
00:15:40,780 --> 00:15:44,320
Scary wolves live
in the forest, you know.

221
00:15:44,530 --> 00:15:46,950
But there's nothing to
worry about now.

222
00:15:47,160 --> 00:15:49,660
We'll be happy to take you...

223
00:15:51,370 --> 00:15:53,460
Thanks, Mister.

224
00:15:53,660 --> 00:15:55,960
I already know the score.

225
00:15:56,920 --> 00:15:59,920
So die, you asshole!

226
00:16:02,090 --> 00:16:05,840
Huh?! What the hell?!

227
00:16:06,050 --> 00:16:09,100
G-Get back here, kid!

228
00:16:15,230 --> 00:16:17,600
You damn animal...!

229
00:16:17,810 --> 00:16:20,110
Die! Die!

230
00:16:20,320 --> 00:16:24,900
This is what you get!
This is what you deserve!

231
00:16:25,110 --> 00:16:28,490
Never get up again!

232
00:16:43,340 --> 00:16:47,840
You're safe now...
You can relax.

233
00:16:50,640 --> 00:16:53,060
I take it you're Mikasa?

234
00:16:53,260 --> 00:16:54,560
I'm Eren.

235
00:16:54,770 --> 00:16:59,900
I'm Dr. Jaeger's son.
I'm sure you've met my dad before.

236
00:17:00,110 --> 00:17:03,270
I was tagging along when he
visited your house for a checkup.

237
00:17:03,480 --> 00:17:05,110
But then...

238
00:17:07,740 --> 00:17:09,950
There were three of them.

239
00:17:19,960 --> 00:17:21,580
Was it you?

240
00:17:24,800 --> 00:17:26,170
Was it you who killed 'em?!

241
00:17:26,380 --> 00:17:27,970
Was it?!

242
00:17:28,170 --> 00:17:31,890
I'm gonna kill you!
I'm gonna kill you!

243
00:17:32,100 --> 00:17:34,810
F-Fight!

244
00:17:35,010 --> 00:17:36,850
Fight!

245
00:17:37,060 --> 00:17:40,650
Fight... or die...!

246
00:17:40,850 --> 00:17:43,060
Win... and live!

247
00:17:43,270 --> 00:17:46,280
What the hell are you thinking, brat?!

248
00:17:46,480 --> 00:17:50,030
The only way to win...
is to fight!

249
00:17:55,540 --> 00:17:57,830
No... I can't do it!

250
00:18:06,550 --> 00:18:10,430
Just then... I remembered.

251
00:18:10,630 --> 00:18:13,300
I had seen this same thing...

252
00:18:13,510 --> 00:18:16,430
...over and over...

253
00:18:16,640 --> 00:18:18,520
...all my life.

254
00:18:20,390 --> 00:18:24,400
I'd seen it everywhere I went...

255
00:18:24,610 --> 00:18:26,020
But...

256
00:18:26,860 --> 00:18:29,570
I always looked the other way.

257
00:18:32,030 --> 00:18:33,450
"That's right...

258
00:18:35,370 --> 00:18:36,990
We live...

259
00:18:38,830 --> 00:18:40,830
...in a cruel world."

260
00:18:49,090 --> 00:18:53,380
At that moment,
my body stopped shaking.

261
00:18:53,590 --> 00:18:58,520
I was in full control of
myself after that.

262
00:19:00,060 --> 00:19:02,770
I thought I could do anything...

263
00:19:02,980 --> 00:19:04,400
"Fight."

264
00:19:09,190 --> 00:19:10,610
"Fight!"

265
00:19:11,490 --> 00:19:12,900
"Fight!"

266
00:19:23,500 --> 00:19:26,710
Stabbed through the heart from behind.

267
00:19:26,920 --> 00:19:29,630
Those kids did this?

268
00:19:34,680 --> 00:19:38,300
Eren. I told you to wait
at the foot of the mountain.

269
00:19:38,510 --> 00:19:41,770
Do you have any idea what you've done?!

270
00:19:41,980 --> 00:19:44,270
I got rid of some dangerous animals!

271
00:19:44,480 --> 00:19:47,230
They just happened to look like people!

272
00:19:47,440 --> 00:19:48,690
Eren!

273
00:19:48,900 --> 00:19:52,940
They would've been long gone
by the time the Military Police arrived!

274
00:19:53,150 --> 00:19:54,570
It would've been too late!

275
00:19:54,780 --> 00:19:59,530
Even so, you were just lucky, Eren!

276
00:19:59,740 --> 00:20:04,870
The way you casually threw
your life away is what I'm angry about!

277
00:20:05,080 --> 00:20:06,960
But...

278
00:20:07,170 --> 00:20:10,380
I wanted to save her as fast as I could...

279
00:20:14,090 --> 00:20:17,550
Mikasa. Do you remember me?

280
00:20:17,760 --> 00:20:21,180
We've met several times before,
when you were little.

281
00:20:23,640 --> 00:20:25,730
Dr. Jaeger...

282
00:20:25,940 --> 00:20:31,150
How do I get home from here?

283
00:20:32,780 --> 00:20:35,110
I'm cold...

284
00:20:35,320 --> 00:20:40,120
I have nowhere to go now...

285
00:20:50,790 --> 00:20:52,800
You can keep this.

286
00:20:56,260 --> 00:20:58,340
Warm, isn't it?

287
00:21:04,180 --> 00:21:06,640
It is...

288
00:21:06,850 --> 00:21:07,980
Mikasa.

289
00:21:08,190 --> 00:21:10,310
Come live with us.

290
00:21:10,520 --> 00:21:12,070
Huh?

291
00:21:12,270 --> 00:21:15,440
You've been through a lot.

292
00:21:15,650 --> 00:21:19,110
You need plenty of rest.

293
00:21:21,200 --> 00:21:22,740
What is it?

294
00:21:22,950 --> 00:21:26,200
C'mon. Let's go already.

295
00:21:26,410 --> 00:21:28,370
To our home.

296
00:21:32,590 --> 00:21:34,420
Yeah. Let's go...

297
00:21:49,440 --> 00:21:54,270
A cruel world in which only
the victors are allowed to live...

298
00:21:58,950 --> 00:22:00,110
Time to withdraw, Ackermann!

299
00:22:00,320 --> 00:22:01,660
Let's scale the wall!

300
00:22:01,860 --> 00:22:03,910
I'll go assist the vanguard's retreat!

301
00:22:04,120 --> 00:22:06,200
H-Hey, Ackermann!

302
00:22:06,410 --> 00:22:11,000
But I do have a place to
call home in this world now.

303
00:22:12,960 --> 00:22:14,210
Eren.

304
00:22:14,420 --> 00:22:18,420
As long as I have you,
I can do anything.

305
00:22:36,480 --> 00:22:41,400
Your dreams are where your heart is

306
00:22:41,610 --> 00:22:47,660
They're more fragile than life itself

307
00:22:47,870 --> 00:22:52,330
Over and over you cast them aside,
only to find more

308
00:22:52,540 --> 00:22:59,010
Now, rest in peace

309
00:22:59,210 --> 00:23:10,350
Pounding impulses defile the things we wish for

310
00:23:10,560 --> 00:23:20,610
and the more we forget
the more we remember again

311
00:23:20,820 --> 00:23:26,570
In this beautiful, cruel world

312
00:23:26,780 --> 00:23:31,750
all I can do is ask why we're still alive

313
00:23:31,950 --> 00:23:37,460
Oh, with our strength... and our weakness...

314
00:23:37,670 --> 00:23:43,130
what are we going to protect if there's no sense

315
00:23:43,340 --> 00:23:46,760
to anything anymore?

316
00:23:53,940 --> 00:23:57,480
"I have a place to call home."

317
00:23:57,690 --> 00:24:01,940
After finishing her rearguard duties,
Mikasa hurries to see Eren,

318
00:24:02,150 --> 00:24:05,133
only to learn of his death.

319
00:24:05,133 --> 00:24:06,160
Small Blade: The Struggle for Trost, Part 3
only to learn of his death.

320
00:24:06,160 --> 00:24:07,010
Small Blade: The Struggle for Trost, Part 3
